The picture below shows how Juan wants to divide a square field into three regions, all sharing a well at vertex $B$. If the side length of the field is $60$ meters, and each of the three regions has the same area, how far must the points $M$ and $N$ be from $D$? Note: The area of each region includes the area occupied by the well.

```latex
\begin{asy}
pair A=(0,0), B=(60,0), C=(60,-60), D=(0,-60), M=(0,-40), N=(20,-60);
pathpen=black;
D(MP("A",A,W)--MP("B",B,NE)--MP("C",C,SE)--MP("D",D,SW)--cycle);
D(B--MP("M",M,W));
D(B--MP("N",N,S));
D(CR(B,3));
\end{asy}
```

Unrelated information has been removed for clarity.

